// Reducer for the silent operand-drop: two operands with no operator
// between them used to resolve to exStack.top() and DROP the rest —
// `var m = { "a" 1 }` compiled to `{ 1 }`, exit 0, wrong value. The
// parseExpression finalize now refuses operand juxtaposition loudly.
// Adjacent STRING literals are unaffected (lexer-level concatenation).
// Oracle: g++ `std::vector<int> v{"a" 1};` -> "expected '}'".
int main()
{
	var m = { "a" 1 };
	return 0;
}
